# examples/ are separate, self-contained npm projects with their own
# tooling -- not part of this package's own format scope, same rationale
# eslint.config.js already uses to exclude them from lint. Each
# test/integration/<category>/<name>/ fixture (relocated out of examples/,
# see examples/README.md) is the same kind of project; only the flat
# <category>/<name>.test.ts wrapper one level up stays in scope.
# benchmarks/performance-runtime and benchmarks/performance-buildtime are
# the same kind of self-contained project too (each its own package.json,
# installed by its own npm install) -- benchmarks/benchmark-fixtures/ and
# the top-level orchestration scripts directly under benchmarks/ stay in
# scope.
